  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Hosea",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 8,
    "summary": "Both Israel and Judah have forsaken the Lord—The Lord has written the great things of His law to Ephraim.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Set the trumpet to thy mouth. He shall come as an eagle against the house of the Lord, because they have transgressed my covenant, and trespassed against my law.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 15,
            "text": "HEB shofar, or ram’s horn."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "Deut. 28:49."
          },
          {
            "start": 105,
            "end": 117,
            "text": "Hosea 6:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 43
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Israel shall cry unto me, My God, we know thee.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "Matt. 7:21 (21–23); Luke 6:46; D&C 112:26."
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "Titus 1:16."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Israel hath cast off the thing that is good: the enemy shall pursue him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 17:5 (1–6, 24)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 38
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They have set up kings, but not by me: they have made princes, and I knew it not: of their silver and their gold have they made them idols, that they may be cut off.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "IE I acknowledged them not."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 76
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thy calf, O Samaria, hath cast thee off; mine anger is kindled against them: how long will it be ere they attain to innocency?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 12:28 (28–30); Acts 7:41."
          },
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 100,
            "text": "OR before they become clean."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 35
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 96
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For from Israel was it also: the workman made it; therefore it is not God: but the calf of Samaria shall be broken in pieces.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 19
          },
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For they have sown the wind, and they shall reap the whirlwind: it hath no stalk: the bud shall yield no meal: if so be it yield, the strangers shall swallow it up.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "Mosiah 7:30; D&C 6:33."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Israel is swallowed up: now shall they be among the Gentiles as a vessel wherein is no pleasure.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "1 Ne. 10:12; Jacob 5:13 (13–14)."
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "Ps. 31:12; Jer. 22:28; 48:38."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 83
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For they are gone up to Assyria, a wild ass alone by himself: Ephraim hath hired lovers.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 31,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 15:19; 17:6 (3–6); Ezek. 23:5."
          },
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "Ezek. 16:33 (33, 41)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, though they have hired among the nations, now will I gather them, and they shall sorrow a little for the burden of the king of princes.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Because Ephraim hath made many altars to sin, altars shall be unto him to sin.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "Ex. 34:13; Hosea 10:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "TG Hypocrisy."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I have written to him the great things of my law, but they were counted as a strange thing.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "TG Scriptures, Writing of."
          },
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "Deut. 4:1, 6 (1–2, 6–8)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "They sacrifice flesh for the sacrifices of mine offerings, and eat it; but the Lord accepteth them not; now will he remember their iniquity, and visit their sins: they shall return to Egypt.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 93,
            "text": "Amos 5:22 (21–22)."
          },
          {
            "start": 116,
            "end": 124,
            "text": "Amos 8:7."
          },
          {
            "start": 184,
            "end": 189,
            "text": "Deut. 28:68 (58–59, 68); Hosea 9:3 (1–3); 11:5."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 24
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 74
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For Israel hath forgotten his Maker, and buildeth temples; and Judah hath multiplied fenced cities: but I will send a fire upon his cities, and it shall devour the palaces thereof.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "Isa. 17:7; 45:9."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "OR palaces or great buildings."
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 91,
            "text": "OR fortified."
          },
          {
            "start": 118,
            "end": 122,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 25:9."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
